
== §1 — CANONICAL RUNTIME VOCABULARY AND DRIFT ==
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_runtime.json
  ✓ schema, version and compiler version are pinned
  ✓ the six navigation modes are declared
  ✓ the eleven interaction actions are declared
  ✓ portal states are exactly OPEN and CLOSED
  ✓ the twelve visibility modes are declared
  ✓ the five measurement types are declared
  ✓ every validation code has a declared severity
  ✓ the model-write refusal code is canonical
  ✓ an unknown code never silently becomes a warning
  ✓ the runtime reuses the canonical visual discipline vocabulary
  ✓ capsule defaults live in the specification, not in code
  ✓ the spec forbids simulation and model-write claims
  ✓ collision behaviour is declared per kind, never inferred

== §2 — DETERMINISTIC RUNTIME SCENE ==
  ✓ the same input produces a byte-identical runtime scene
  ✓ every fixture compiles to a valid runtime scene
  ✓ the runtime scene references its visual source
  ✓ the runtime id derives from the source scene id
  ✓ writes_to_model is structurally false on every scene
  ✓ a configuration requesting writes_to_model is refused
  ✓ compiling does not mutate the visual scene
  ✓ compiling does not mutate the source model
  ✓ the runtime scene carries no timestamp
  ✓ runtime ids are deterministic and prefixed by kind
  ✓ runtime object ids are unique
  ✓ objects are sorted deterministically
  ✓ a duplicate source object id is rejected, not merged
  ✓ a missing source scene is rejected
  ✓ an invalid source scene is rejected
  ✓ a failed compile still returns a well-formed empty scene

== §3 — SOURCE TRACEABILITY ==
  ✓ every model-derived runtime object names its source element
  ✓ every runtime object records its source scene
  ✓ a visual-only object gains no engineering source
  ✓ every obstacle traces back to a runtime object
  ✓ every walkable surface traces back to a canonical space
  ✓ every portal traces back to a modelled door

== §4 — RUNTIME SCENE AND RUNTIME STATE ARE SEPARATE ==
  ✓ the state is a distinct object with its own fields
  ✓ the state carries no compiled geometry
  ✓ the state declares writes_to_model false
  ✓ the state references the scene by id only
  ✓ mutating the state does not touch the scene
  ✓ simulation time starts at zero and advances deterministically
  ✓ a negative or non-finite time delta is refused
  ✓ no simulation engine is attached to the clock

== §5 — RULE INPUTS AND SUMMARY ==
  ✓ rule inputs are runtime counts only
  ✓ no runtime count is compared to a threshold
  ✓ the summary declares no engineering geometry was modified
  ✓ the summary declares compliance NOT_EVALUATED
  ✓ counts agree with the compiled collections

